{
  "id": "09317_daburu",
  "headword": "ダブる",
  "reading": "だぶる",
  "part_of_speech": "godan verb",
  "gloss": "to repeat a grade; to overlap; to duplicate",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "godan",
    "ending": "る",
    "stem": "ダブ"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to repeat a grade; to be held back",
      "explanation": "To fail to advance to the next school year and have to repeat the same grade."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to overlap; to duplicate; to double up",
      "explanation": "For things to be duplicated or for schedules to conflict."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "09317_daburu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{大学|だいがく}でダブった。",
      "english": "I had to repeat a year in college.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "09317_daburu_ex2",
      "japanese": "このまま{行|い}くとダブるかも。",
      "english": "At this rate, I might have to repeat the year.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "09317_daburu_ex3",
      "japanese": "ダブらないように{頑張|がんば}る。",
      "english": "I'll work hard so I don't have to repeat.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "09317_daburu_ex4",
      "japanese": "{予定|よてい}がダブっている。",
      "english": "My schedules are overlapping.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "09317_daburu_ex5",
      "japanese": "カードがダブった。",
      "english": "I got a duplicate card.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "09317_daburu_ex6",
      "japanese": "{同|おな}じ{本|ほん}がダブって{買|か}ってしまった。",
      "english": "I accidentally bought the same book twice.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "ダブる comes from the English word \"double.\" It's a casual verb formed by adding る to the loanword.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is casual/colloquial language. For sense 1, formal alternatives include {留年|りゅうねん}する. For sense 2, use {重複|ちょうふく}する or {重|かさ}なる.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ダブる: to repeat/overlap\n- ダブり: duplication (noun form)\n- {予定|よてい}がダブる: schedules conflict",
